Package: yunmai-noble-desktop
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Homepage: https://github.com/Vanuan/yunmai-noble
Depends: fontconfig, libc6 (>= @LIBC@), libfreetype6, libgcc-s1, libxau6, libxcb-xkb1, libxcb1, libxdmcp6, libxkbcommon-x11-0, libxkbcommon0
Breaks: yunmai-noble (<< @VERSION@)
Replaces: yunmai-noble (<< @VERSION@)
Recommends: fonts-dejavu-core, libgl1 | libvulkan1, yunmai-noble (= @VERSION@)
Suggests: yunmai-noble-simulator
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Description: GPUI dashboard and simulator control for Yunmai Noble
 The yunmai-noble-desktop application shows the latest measurement, the
 live scale state, and the measurement history, and it selects which
 suite driver is active through the Settings dialog. It also ships
 yunmai-noble-simulator-ui, the standalone virtual-scale control app.
 .
 The client talks to the suite API over HTTP, so it can point at a
 remote historian with --historian or YUNMAI_HISTORIAN_URL. Installing
 yunmai-noble locally makes the default 127.0.0.1:3000 work and lets the
 client start the service on demand.
